 2119                  *
 2120                  *LOCAL VARIABLE STORAGE FOR THE PURGE FUNCTION
 2121                  *
 2122 0F59             PUUID  RMB    1                SAVE LOCATION FOR DISK UNIT I/D BEING PURGED
 2123 0F5A             PUFCP  RMB    2                FILE CONTROL BLOCK STRING POINTER (FILE BEING PURGED)
 2124 0F5C             PUSEC  RMB    1                CURRENT SECTOR BEING PURGED <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2125 0F5D             PUFMP  RMB    2                FILE CONTROL BLOCK STRING POINTER (FILE BEING MOVED)
 2126 0F5F             PUSEM  RMB    1                CURRENT SECTOR BEING MOVED <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2127                  *
 2128                  *
 2129                  *USER PROMPT MESSAGE STRINGS FOR THE PURGE FUNCTION
 2130                  *
 2131 0F60 0A          PERMM  FCB    $0A
 2132 0F61 20 50 45 52        FCC    / PERMANENT/
    + 0F65 4D 41 4E 45
    + 0F69 4E 54
 2133 0F6B 07          PURGM  FCB    $07
 2134 0F6C 20 50 55 52        FCC    / PURGED/
    + 0F70 47 45 44
 2135 0F73 0C          PKDSM  FCB    $0C
 2136 0F74 50 41 43 4B        FCC    /PACKING DISK/
    + 0F78 49 4E 47 20
    + 0F7C 44 49 53 4B
 2137                         PAGE                    THIS PROGRAM WAS COMMENTED BY THE AUSTRALIAN 6800 USER'S GROUP
 2138                  *
 2139                  *THIS FUNCTION PURGES UNWANTED FILES FROM THE DISK, AND
 2140                  *PACKS THE REMAINING FILES, RECLAIMING THE SPACE
 2141                  *
 2142                  *PURGE IS DONE IN TWO PASSES
 2143                  *
 2144                  *                     PASS 1
 2145                  *TEST VALIDITY OF INPUT FILE STRING, WRITE DELETED FILE
 2146                  *MARKERS IN DIRECTORY FCB OF FILES TO BE PURGED.
 2147                  *
 2148                  *                     PASS 2
 2149                  *SEARCH FOR DELETED FILE MARK (ATTRIBUTE = 80).  ON FINDING
 2150                  *THE FIRST DELETED FILE MARK, SCAN FORWARD UNTIL A NON-
 2151                  *DELETED FILE IS FOUND. THIS FILE IS THEN MOVED INTO THE
 2152                  *AREA TO BE PURGED.  THIS PROCESS THEN CONTINUES TO THE END
 2153                  *OF THE DIRECTORY. EACH TIME A FILE IS MOVED, THE DIRECTORY
 2154                  *IS UPDATED.
 2155                  *
 2156                  *                    ERRORS
 2157                  *SEVERAL ERRORS MAY OCCUR DURING THE PURGE PROCESS, SOME OF
 2158                  *WHICH ARE FATAL TO ALL FILES FOLLOWING THE ERROR.  SOME
 2159                  *POSSIBLE ERRORS MAY CAUSE DIRECTORY FAULTS.  PURGE SHOULD
 2160                  *NOT BE USED ON A DISK THAT HAS NO BACKUP COPY.
 2161                  *
 2162      0F80        PURGE  EQU    *
 2163 0F80 96 C5              LDAA   FLNM5            GET THE UNIT I/D TO BE PURGED
 2164 0F82 B7 0F59            STAA   PUUID            AND DEFINE THE PURGE UID
 2165 0F85 BD 0367     PURG1  JSR    PRSFL            PARSE THE NEXT FILE NAME
 2166 0F88 96 C0              LDAA   FLNM0            GET THE FIRST CHARACTER
 2167 0F8A 81 20              CMPA   #SPC             IF IT IS A SPACE
 2168 0F8C 26 03              BNE    PURG2            THEN
 2169 0F8E 7E 1031            JMP    PKDSK            FILE INPUT IS COMPLETE
 2170                  *
 2171 0F91 B6 0F59     PURG2  LDAA   PUUID            PICK UP THE PURGE UID
 2172 0F94 97 C5              STAA   FLNM5            AND DEFINE THIS FILE TO RESIDE ON PURGE UID DRIVE
 2173 0F96 BD 0533            JSR    DFINF            DEFINE THE INPUT FILE
 2174 0F99 4D                 TSTA                    IF SUCCESSFUL
 2175 0F9A 26 E9              BNE    PURG1            THEN
 2176 0F9C A6 05              LDAA   $5,X             GET THE ATTRIBUTE ENTRY
 2177 0F9E 81 01              CMPA   #$1              IF THE ATTRIBUTE IS NOT "PERMANENT" (01)
 2178 0FA0 26 16              BNE    PURG3            THEN
 2179                  *
 2180 0FA2 CE 00C0            LDX    #FLNM0           SET A POINTER TO THE FILE NAME
 2181 0FA5 C6 05              LDAB   #$5              WITH A CHARACTER COUNT OF 5
 2182 0FA7 BD 03BA            JSR    PRINS            PRINT OUT THE FILE NAME
 2183 0FAA CE 0F61            LDX    #PERMM+1         POINT TO MESSAGE STRING & SET CHAR
 2184 0FAD F6 0F60            LDAB   PERMM            COUNT FOR PERMANENT MESSAGE
 2185 0FB0 BD 03BA            JSR    PRINS            PRINT " PERMANENT"
 2186 0FB3 BD 03C4            JSR    CRLF             PRINT <CR><LF> FOR NEW LINE ON PRINTER
 2187 0FB6 20 CD              BRA    PURG1            CONTINUE WITH NEXT FILE
 2188                  *
 2189 0FB8 86 80       PURG3  LDAA   #$80             DEFINE A "DELETED FILE" MARK
 2190 0FBA A7 05              STAA   $5,X             SET FILE ATTRIBUTE "DELETED" IN FCB
 2191 0FBC B6 0150            LDAA   USECT            PICK UP THE DIRECTORY <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2192 0FBF 5F                 CLRB                    SELECT TRACK 0 FOR DIRECTORY
 2193 0FC0 CE 00D0            LDX    #SECB1           SET A POINTER TO THE SECTOR BUFFER
 2194 0FC3 BD 0480            JSR    WRTSE            WRITE THIS SECTOR TO DISK
 2195 0FC6 4D                 TSTA                    IF DIRECTORY SECTOR WRITE FAILURE
 2196 0FC7 27 03              BEQ    PURG4            THEN
 2197 0FC9 7E 0435            JMP    MEDER            PRINT "MEDIA ERROR" & WAIT FOR NEW COMMAND
 2198                  *
 2199 0FCC CE 00C0     PURG4  LDX    #FLNM0           SET A POINTER TO THE FILE NAME
 2200 0FCF C6 05              LDAB   #$5              WITH A CHARACTER COUNT OF 5
 2201 0FD1 BD 03BA            JSR    PRINS            PRINT OUT THE FILE NAME
 2202 0FD4 CE 0F6C            LDX    #PURGM+1         POINT TO MESSAGE STRING & SET CHAR
 2203 0FD7 F6 0F6B            LDAB   PURGM            COUNT FOR PURGED MESSAGE
 2204 0FDA BD 03BA            JSR    PRINS            PRINT " PURGED"
 2205 0FDD BD 03C4            JSR    CRLF             PRINT <CR><LF> FOR NEW LINE ON PRINTER
 2206 0FE0 20 A3              BRA    PURG1            CONTINUE WITH NEXT FILE
 2207                  *
 2208                  *
 2209 0FE2 0C          DIRSE  CLC                     CLEAR "C" BIT FOR SHIFTING
 2210 0FE3 B6 0F59            LDAA   PUUID            PICK UP PURGE UNIT I/D
 2211 0FE6 46                 RORA                    SHIFT UID BITS INTO BITS 6 &7
 2212 0FE7 46                 RORA                    ROTATING THEM THROUGH THE C BIT
 2213 0FE8 46                 RORA                    BIT 7 BECOMES OLD 1, BIT 6 BECOMES OLD 0
 2214 0FE9 8A 04              ORAA   #$4              THE DIRECTORY STARTS AT SECTOR 4
 2215 0FEB B7 0F5F            STAA   PUSEM            DEFINE THE PURGE DIRECTORY <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2216                  *
 2217 0FEE CE 00D0     DIRS1  LDX    #SECB1           LOAD POINTER FOR SECTOR BUFFER
 2218 0FF1 FF 0F5D            STX    PUFMP            INITIALIZE THE SECTOR SCAN
 2219                  *
 2220 0FF4 B6 0F5F     DIRS2  LDAA   PUSEM            GET CURRENT <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2221 0FF7 84 3F              ANDA   #$3F             MASK TO SECTOR ONLY (STRIP OFF UID)
 2222 0FF9 81 1B              CMPA   #27              IF THIS IS THE END OF TRACK (26 SECTORS/TRACK)
 2223 0FFB 26 03              BNE    DIRS3            THEN
 2224 0FFD 86 FF              LDAA   #$FF             FLAG END OF DIRECTORY
 2225 0FFF 39                 RTS                     AND RETURN TO CALLER
 2226                  *
 2227 1000 CE 00D0     DIRS3  LDX    #SECB1           START AT THE BEGINNING OF THE SECTOR BUFFER
 2228 1003 B6 0F5F            LDAA   PUSEM            GET CURRENT <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2229 1006 5F                 CLRB                    SELECT TRACK 0 FOR THE DIRECTORY
 2230 1007 BD 0408            JSR    RED11            READ IN THE DIRECTORY SECTOR
 2231 100A 4D                 TSTA                    IF A "DD" MARK WAS FOUND IN THIS SECTOR
 2232 100B 27 05              BEQ    DIRS5            THEN
 2233 100D 7C 0F5F     DIRS4  INC    PUSEM            TAKE THE NEXT SECTOR
 2234 1010 20 DC              BRA    DIRS1            AND TRY IT
 2235                  *
 2236 1012 FE 0F5D     DIRS5  LDX    PUFMP            USE THE CURRENT SECTOR POINTER
 2237 1015 A6 05              LDAA   $5,X             READ THE ATTRIBUTE VALUE FROM THE CURRENT FCB
 2238 1017 39                 RTS                     AND RETURN TO CALLER
 2239                  *
 2240                  *
 2241                  *ADVANCE BUFFER POINTER BY 11 TO NEXT FCB.
 2242                  *WHEN NEEDED, GET NEXT DIRECTORY SECTOR
 2243                  *
 2244 1018 86 0B       NXFCB  LDAA   #11              DEFINE 11 BYTES IN A FILE CONTROL BLOCK
 2245 101A 5F                 CLRB                    WITH A HIGH BYTE OF 0
 2246 101B BB 0F5E            ADDA   PUFMP+LBYT       ADD 11 TO LOW BYTE OF POINTER
 2247 101E F9 0F5D            ADCB   PUFMP            ADD IN THE CARRY (IF ANY) TO THE HIGH BYTE
 2248 1021 B7 0F5E            STAA   PUFMP+LBYT       STORE THE LOW POINTER BYTE
 2249 1024 F7 0F5D            STAB   PUFMP            AND THE HIGH POINTER BYTE (POINTER IS NOW +11)
 2250 1027 FE 0F5D            LDX    PUFMP            USE THE NEW POINTER VALUE (NEXT FCB)
 2251 102A 8C 0149            CPX    #SECB1+121       IF THERE ARE NO MORE FCB'S IN THIS SECTOR
 2252 102D 26 C5              BNE    DIRS2            THEN
 2253 102F 20 DC              BRA    DIRS4            TAKE THE NEXT SECTOR & FIRST FCB IN THAT SECTOR
 2254                  *
 2255                  *
 2256                  *SEARCH DIRECTORY FOR FILES TO BE PURGED (ATTRIBUTE = $80)
 2257                  *
 2258 1031 CE 0F74     PKDSK  LDX    #PKDSM+1         LOAD POINTER TO MESSAGE STRING
 2259 1034 F6 0F73            LDAB   PKDSM            LOAD THE CHARACTER COUNT
 2260 1037 BD 03BA            JSR    PRINS            PRINT "PACKING DISK"
 2261 103A BD 03C4            JSR    CRLF             PRINT <CR><LF> FOR NEW LINE
 2262 103D BD 0FE2            JSR    DIRSE            READ & SET UP THE FIRST DIRECTORY SECTOR
 2263                  *
 2264 1040 81 FF       PKDS1  CMPA   #$FF             IF THIS IS THE END OF THE DIRECTORY TRACK
 2265 1042 26 01              BNE    PKDS2            THEN
 2266 1044 39                 RTS                     RETURN
 2267 1045 81 80       PKDS2  CMPA   #$80             IF ATTRIBUTE OF CURRENT FCB IS NOT "DELETED FILE" ($80
 2268 1047 27 05              BEQ    PURFL            THEN
 2269 1049 BD 1018            JSR    NXFCB            LOOK AT THE NEXT FCB
 2270 104C 20 F2              BRA    PKDS1            AND CONTINUE
 2271                  *
 2272                  *PURGE THIS FILE, MOVE THE FILES, UPDATE THE DIRECTORY
 2273                  *
 2274 104E FE 0F5D     PURFL  LDX    PUFMP            GET POINTER TO CURRENT FCB
 2275 1051 A6 06              LDAA   $6,X             GET THE STARTING TRACK ADDRESS OF FILE TO BE PURGED
 2276 1053 97 0B              STAA   OTRK             DEFINE IT AS START OF AN OUTPUT FILE
 2277 1055 B6 0F59            LDAA   PUUID            GET PURGE UNIT NUMBER
 2278 1058 97 02              STAA   OUNIT            DEFINE OUTPUT FILE ON THAT UNIT
 2279 105A 0C                 CLC                     CLEAR THE "C" BIT FOR SHIFTING
 2280 105B 46                 RORA                    SHIFT THE UID INTO BITS 6 & 7
 2281 105C 46                 RORA                    SHIFTING THROUGH THE CARRY BIT
 2282 105D 46                 RORA                    BIT 7 BECOMES OLD 1, BIT 6 BECOMES OLD 0
 2283 105E AA 07              ORAA   $7,X             INCLUDE THE START SECTOR OF THE FILE TO BE PURGED
 2284 1060 97 0C              STAA   OSCTR            DEFINE AS THE OUTPUT FILE <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2285 1062 7F 000D            CLR    OCNTR            CLEAR THE BYTE COUNTER FOR THE OUTPUT FILE
 2286 1065 CE 07B7            LDX    #1975            DEFINE A FILE SIZE OF ALL USER SPACE ON DISK
 2287 1068 DF 09              STX    OSIZE            AS THE OUTPUT FILE SIZE (SHUT OFF FILE SIZE MONITOR)
 2288 106A DF C7              STX    FILRQ            REQUEST A FILE SIZE OF ALL USER SPACE
 2289 106C FE 0F5D            LDX    PUFMP            GET POINTER TO CURRENT FCB
 2290 106F FF 0F5A            STX    PUFCP            SAVE IT FOR LATER USE
 2291 1072 B6 0F5F            LDAA   PUSEM            GET THE CURRENT DIRECTORY <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2292 1075 B7 0F5C            STAA   PUSEC            SAVE IT FOR USE LATER
 2293                  *
 2294 1078 BD 1018     PURF1  JSR    NXFCB            TAKE THE NEXT FILE CONTROL BLOCK
 2295 107B 81 FF              CMPA   #$FF             IF THIS IS NOT THE END OF THE DIRECTORY TRACK
 2296 107D 27 36              BEQ    PURF3            AND
 2297 107F 81 80              CMPA   #$80             IF THIS IS NOT ANOTHER DELETED FILE
 2298 1081 27 F5              BEQ    PURF1            THEN
 2299                  *
 2300 1083 FE 0F5D            LDX    PUFMP            POINT TO THE CURRENT FILE CONTROL BLOCK
 2301 1086 A6 06              LDAA   $6,X             PICK UP THIS FILE'S STARTING TRACK ADDRESS
 2302 1088 97 06              STAA   ITRK             DEFINE THIS AS AN INPUT FILE TRACK START ADDRESS
 2303 108A A6 08              LDAA   $8,X             PICK UP THIS FILE'S LENGTH (HIGH BYTE)
 2304 108C 97 04              STAA   ISIZE            DEFINE AS INPUT FILE SIZE (HIGH BYTE)
 2305 108E A6 09              LDAA   $9,X             PICK UP THIS FILE'S LENGTH (LOW BYTE)
 2306 1090 97 05              STAA   ISIZE+LBYT       DEFINE AS INPUT FILE SIZE (LOW BYTE)
 2307 1092 7F 0008            CLR    ICNTR            CLEAR THE INPUT FILE BYTE COUNTER
 2308 1095 B6 0F59            LDAA   PUUID            GET PURGE UNIT NUMBER
 2309 1098 0C                 CLC                     CLEAR THE "C" BIT FOR SHIFTING
 2310 1099 46                 RORA                    SHIFT THE UID INTO BITS 6 & 7
 2311 109A 46                 RORA                    ROTATING THEM THROUGH THE CARRY BIT
 2312 109B 46                 RORA                    BIT 7 BECOMES OLD 1, BIT 6 BECOMES OLD 0
 2313 109C AA 07              ORAA   $7,X             INCLUDE SECTOR TO MAKE <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2314 109E 4A                 DECA                    MINUS ONE
 2315 109F 97 07              STAA   ISCTR            AS THE STARTING SECTOR FOR AN INPUT FILE
 2316 10A1 0C                 CLC                     CLEAR THE "C" BIT FOR SHIFTING
 2317 10A2 49                 ROLA                    SHIFT UID BACK INTO BITS 1 & 0
 2318 10A3 49                 ROLA                    SECTOR NUMBER NOW OCCUPIES BITS 3 - 7
 2319 10A4 49                 ROLA                    (SECTOR NUMBER IS * 8)
 2320 10A5 97 03              STAA   IUNIT            SAVE THIS AS INPUT UNIT <SECTOR><UNIT>
 2321 10A7 BD 0F24            JSR    MOVFL            MOVE THE INPUT FILE INTO SPACE CREATED BY PURGING
 2322 10AA 7D 000D     PURF2  TST    OCNTR            IF OUTPUT SECTOR NOT COMPLETE
 2323 10AD 27 09              BEQ    PURF4            THEN
 2324 10AF 4F                 CLRA                    DEFINE A NULL
 2325 10B0 BD E80C            JSR    XWRT             PAD THE REMAINDER OF THIS SECTOR WITH NULLS
 2326 10B3 20 F5              BRA    PURF2            WHILE SECTOR, CONTINUE
 2327                  *
 2328 10B5 7E 116D     PURF3  JMP    WTEOD            CLOSE END OF DIRECTORY (BRANCH RANGE EXTENSION)
 2329                  *
 2330                  *
 2331                  *UPDATE THE FCB NOW RELATING TO THE FILE JUST MOVED
 2332                  *
 2333 10B8 FE 0F5D     PURF4  LDX    PUFMP            SET THE POINTER TO THE FCB OF THE FILE JUST MOVED
 2334 10BB A6 05              LDAA   $5,X             GET FILE ATTRIBUTE
 2335 10BD 36                 PSHA                    AND SAVE IT
 2336 10BE A6 04              LDAA   $4,X             GET NAME CHAR #5
 2337 10C0 36                 PSHA                    AND SAVE IT
 2338 10C1 A6 03              LDAA   $3,X             GET NAME CHAR #4
 2339 10C3 36                 PSHA                    AND SAVE IT
 2340 10C4 A6 02              LDAA   $2,X             GET NAME CHAR #3
 2341 10C6 36                 PSHA                    AND SAVE IT
 2342 10C7 A6 01              LDAA   $1,X             GET NAME CHAR #2
 2343 10C9 36                 PSHA                    AND SAVE IT
 2344 10CA A6 00              LDAA   $0,X             GET NAME CHAR #1
 2345 10CC 36                 PSHA                    AND SAVE IT
 2346                  *
 2347 10CD D6 C7              LDAB   FILRQ            GET THE CURRENT "MAXIMUM USER DISK SPACE"
 2348 10CF 96 C8              LDAA   FILRQ+LBYT       (IT STARTED OUT AS 1975 SECTORS)
 2349 10D1 90 0A              SUBA   OSIZE+LBYT       SUBTRACT THE SECTORS NOT USED DURING
 2350 10D3 D2 09              SBCB   OSIZE            WRITE, GIVING THIS FILE'S SECTOR COUNT
 2351 10D5 8B 01              ADDA   #$1              OR SIZE, AFTER ALLOWING ONE MORE SECTOR
 2352 10D7 C9 00              ADCB   #$0              WITH PROPAGATED CARRY
 2353 10D9 37                 PSHB                    SAVE FILE SIZE (HIGH)
 2354 10DA 36                 PSHA                    SAVE FILE SIZE (LOW)
 2355                  *
 2356 10DB CE 00D0            LDX    #SECB1           POINT TO THE DIRECTORY SECTOR BUFFER
 2357 10DE B6 0F5C            LDAA   PUSEC            GET <UNIT><SECTOR> FOR PURGED FILE FCB
 2358 10E1 5F                 CLRB                    USE TRACK 0 FOR DIRECTORY READ
 2359 10E2 BD 0408            JSR    RED11            READ THE DIRECTORY SECTOR
 2360                  *
 2361                  *AN ERROR CHECK HAS BEEN MISSED HERE!!!!
 2362                  *
 2363 10E5 FE 0F5A            LDX    PUFCP            POINT TO THE CURRENT PURGED FILE FCB
 2364 10E8 32                 PULA                    GET LOW BYTE OF MOVED FILE SIZE
 2365 10E9 A7 09              STAA   $9,X             STORE IT AS FCB LENGTH (LOW)
 2366 10EB 32                 PULA                    GET HIGH BYTE OF MOVED FILE SIZE
 2367 10EC A7 08              STAA   $8,X             STORE IT AS FCB LENGTH (HIGH)
 2368 10EE 32                 PULA                    GET THE FIRST CHAR OF THE MOVED FILE NAME
 2369 10EF A7 00              STAA   $0,X             STORE IT AS FCB NAME, CHAR 1
 2370 10F1 32                 PULA                    GET THE SECOND CHAR OF THE MOVED FILE NAME
 2371 10F2 A7 01              STAA   $1,X             STORE IT AS FCB NAME, CHAR 2
 2372 10F4 32                 PULA                    GET THE THIRD CHAR OF THE MOVED FILE NAME
 2373 10F5 A7 02              STAA   $2,X             STORE IT AS FCB NAME, CHAR 3
 2374 10F7 32                 PULA                    GET THE FOURTH CHAR OF THE MOVED FILE NAME
 2375 10F8 A7 03              STAA   $3,X             STORE IT AS FCB NAME, CHAR 4
 2376 10FA 32                 PULA                    GET THE FIFTH CHAR OF THE MOVED FILE NAME
 2377 10FB A7 04              STAA   $4,X             STORE IT AS FCB NAME, CHAR 5
 2378 10FD 32                 PULA                    GET THE ATTRIBUTE CHARACTER OF THE MOVED FILE
 2379 10FE A7 05              STAA   $5,X             STORE IT AS FCB ATTRIBUTE CHAR
 2380                  *
 2381                  *FCB IS NOW UPDATED (TRACK & SECTOR ARE KNOWN TO BE CORRECT)
 2382                  *
 2383 1100 CE 00D0            LDX    #SECB1           POINT TO THE BEGINNING OF THE SECTOR BUFFER
 2384 1103 B6 0F5C            LDAA   PUSEC            GET THE <UNIT><SECTOR> FOR THIS FCB ENTRY
 2385 1106 5F                 CLRB                    SELECT TRACK 0 FOR THE DIRECTORY
 2386 1107 BD 0480            JSR    WRTSE            WRITE THIS SECTOR TO DISK
 2387 110A 4D                 TSTA                    IF THERE WAS A WRITE ERROR
 2388 110B 27 03              BEQ    PURF5            THEN
 2389 110D 7E 0435            JMP    MEDER            PRINT "MEDIA ERROR" & WAIT FOR NEW COMMAND
 2390                  *
 2391 1110 B6 0F5D     PURF5  LDAA   PUFMP            GET POINTER TO CURRENT FCB (HIGH BYTE)
 2392 1113 36                 PSHA                    AND SAVE IT
 2393 1114 B6 0F5E            LDAA   PUFMP+LBYT       GET POINTER TO CURRENT FCB (LOW BYTE)
 2394 1117 36                 PSHA                    AND SAVE IT
 2395 1118 B6 0F5F            LDAA   PUSEM            GET CURRENT FCB <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2396 111B 36                 PSHA                    AND SAVE IT
 2397 111C FE 0F5A            LDX    PUFCP            GET THE POINTER FOR FCB OF THE PURGED FILE
 2398 111F FF 0F5D            STX    PUFMP            AND SAVE IT AS TARGET FOR FCB MOVE
 2399 1122 B6 0F5C            LDAA   PUSEC            GET THE <UNIT><SECTOR> FOR FCB OF THE PURGED FILE
 2400 1125 B7 0F5F            STAA   PUSEM            AND SAVE IT AS TARGET FOR FCB MOVE
 2401 1128 BD 1018            JSR    NXFCB            GET THE NEXT FCB
 2402 112B FE 0F5D            LDX    PUFMP            POINT TO IT IN THE SECTOR BUFFER
 2403 112E 96 0B              LDAA   OTRK             GET THE LAST TRACK USED
 2404 1130 A7 06              STAA   $6,X             SAVE IT AS START TRACK IN THE NEW FCB
 2405 1132 96 0C              LDAA   OSCTR            GET THE LAST <UNIT><SECTOR> USED
 2406 1134 84 3F              ANDA   #$3F             STRIP OFF THE UNIT ID BITS
 2407 1136 A7 07              STAA   $7,X             SAVE IT AS START SECTOR IN THE NEW FCB
 2408 1138 CE 00D0            LDX    #SECB1           START AT THE BEGINNING OF THE SECTOR BUFFER
 2409 113B B6 0F5F            LDAA   PUSEM            GET THE <UNIT><SECTOR> FOR THE CHANGED FCB
 2410 113E 5F                 CLRB                    SELECT TRACK 0 FOR THE DIRECTORY
 2411 113F BD 0480            JSR    WRTSE            WRITE THIS SECTOR TO DISK
 2412 1142 4D                 TSTA                    IF THERE WAS A WRITE ERROR
 2413 1143 27 03              BEQ    PURF7            THEN
 2414 1145 7E 0435     PURF6  JMP    MEDER            PRINT "MEDIA ERROR" & WAIT FOR NEW COMMAND
 2415 1148 CE 07B7     PURF7  LDX    #1975            DEFINE MAXIMUM USER SPACE AVAILABLE ON DISK
 2416 114B DF 09              STX    OSIZE            SET AN OUTPUT SIZE OF MAX. (SHUT OFF OUTPUT TEST)
 2417 114D DF C7              STX    FILRQ            REQUEST A OUTPUT FILE OF MAXIMUM USER SPACE
 2418 114F 7F 000D            CLR    OCNTR            CLEAR THE OUTPUT FILE BYTE COUNTER
 2419 1152 FE 0F5D            LDX    PUFMP            GO BACK TO THE PURGED FILE FCB
 2420 1155 FF 0F5A            STX    PUFCP            IN THE SAVE LOCATION
 2421 1158 B6 0F5F            LDAA   PUSEM            GO BACK TO THE PURGED FILE <UNIT><SECTOR>
 2422 115B B7 0F5C            STAA   PUSEC            IN THE SAVE LOCATION
 2423 115E 32                 PULA                    GET CURRENT <UNIT><SECTOR> OFF STACK
 2424 115F B7 0F5F            STAA   PUSEM            AND RESTORE IT
 2425 1162 32                 PULA                    GET LOW BYTE OF CURRENT FCB PONTER OFF STACK
 2426 1163 B7 0F5E            STAA   PUFMP+LBYT       AND RESTORE IT
 2427 1166 32                 PULA                    GET HIGH BYTE OF CURRENT FCB POINTER OFF STACK
 2428 1167 B7 0F5D            STAA   PUFMP            AND RESTORE IT
 2429 116A 7E 1078            JMP    PURF1            CONTINUE THE PACKING PROCESS
